flow is jakub's own work, with the following upstream contributions.

PORTED SCRIPT
-------------

    scripts/worktree-audit.sh

which is ported from Lauren Tan's "pstack" plugin in Cursor's plugin repo
(https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack, skills/poteto-mode/scripts/
worktree-audit.sh, upstream commit 99559f2f52047978602ef365589275831e76af07), MIT.
Local changes: Linux `stat -c`, Claude Code transcript layout under
~/.claude/projects/<slug>/, a `review` bucket for unpushed work, and the bucket
rename verify-recent-chat → verify-recent-session. The MIT licence text is reproduced below.

SUPPORTING SKILLS
-----------------

skills/how/SKILL.md and skills/hillclimb/ draw on Lauren Tan's pstack workflows:

    https://github.com/cursor/plugins
    upstream commit c1c0a32802223f4be824112dd83d33ad29a8b26c
    pstack/skills/how/SKILL.md
    pstack/skills/poteto-mode/playbooks/hillclimb.md
    pstack/skills/show-me-your-work/SKILL.md

These are locally authored adaptations, not vendored copies or a patch series.
The Flow versions use the charter's delegation and review rules, interactive experiment
setup, retained candidate branches, and a batch wait before sequential measurements.
The how skill adds focused runtime investigation and reports concerns encountered.
The experiment record is local to Flow. No Cursor agents, scripts, or runtime are included.
The same upstream MIT licence applies and is retained below. Future changes are local edits.

